  "Roachford - Cuddly Toy": "[Verse]\n\n\n   F                         Eb/G\nI know you've heard so many people say\n             Eb/Bb                  Bb\nI've got a different girl in every town.\n\n           F                    Eb/G\nBut there must be somebody telling lies\n      Eb/Bb                  Bb\nAnd spreading rumours\nSpreading rumours all around.\n\n              F                         Eb/G\nBecause my only joy is a cuddly toy\n    Eb/Bb                  Bb\nWaiting for me when I get home.\n\n   F                  Eb/G          Eb/Bb                  Bb\nAnd what I need is a girl like you to call my very own.\n\n[Chorus]\n                   GM\nSo you've got to feel for me\nBaby\nGM    F/Bb    C\n feel for me   Baby\n\n\n                                  Gm    F/Bb    C    D/F#\nYeah You've got to feel for me baby   - feel for me     Baby -\n\n\n                                   Gm    F/Bb    C\nYeah You've got to feel for me baby    - feel for me Baby -\n\n\n           Eb  F\nOh Gimme some love.\n\n[Verse]\n\n       F\nWell I don't pou out my heart like this\n        Eb/G          Eb/Bb                  Bb\nTo everyone and not anyone that I meet.\n       F                              Eb/G\nAnd I know it ain't the wine ' cause I feel just fine\n          Eb/Bb                       Bb\nCan't you see Baby I'm still on my feet!\n\n           F\nOh But a cuddly toy\n             Eb/G\nThat's my only joy\n             Eb/Bb              Bb\nWaiting for me when I get home.\n       F              Eb/G             Eb/Bb            Bb\nAnd what I need is a girl like you to call my very own.\n\n[Chorus]\n                  Gm\nSo you've got to feel for me\nBaby\nGm    F/Bb    C\n feel for me   Baby\n\n\n                                  Gm    F/Bb    C    D/F#\nYeah You've got to feel for me baby   - feel for me     Baby -\n\n\n                                   Gm    F/Bb    C\nYeah You've got to feel for me baby    - feel for me Baby -\n\n[Solo]\n Bbm 