  "Sea Urchins - Time Is All I've Seen": "D / Dsus4 / D\n\nD  Am          G\nI opened up my window\nD  Am          G\nWoah oh I opened up my mind\nD / Dsus4 / D\nTo what was outside\n\nG\nAnd those thoughts are flying\nA\nThat I never caught\nG\nIn a sea of stories\nA\nWas waiting to retort\nG\nMaybe imagination\nA\nAll within a dream\nG\nCause life is where I'm going\n                A\nAnd time is all I've seen\n\nBorn within a dream\nD / Dsus4 / D\n\nD  Am          G\nI stepped into my garden\nD  Am          G\nWoah oh I stepped into my mind\nD  Am          G\nWhat I could find\n\nD / Dsus4 / D\n\nG                     A\nAll the tangle from a tiny seed\nG                     A\nIt gets its space on every little thing it meets\nG                     A\nYou take the path where other may lead\nG\nCause where life is where I'm going\n                A\nAnd time is all I've seen\n\nWherever it may lead\n\nD / Dsus4 / D\n",
  "Shed Seven - Going For Gold": "A D / A D / A D / A D\n\n[Verse 1]\nA D\nI never said never ever\nA D\nYou took the words right out of my mouth\nA D\nIs the sea your sunshine\nA D\nHave you been told\nD\nThe sea is your lifeline\nG D\nGoing for gold\nG\nYou took the words right out of my mouth\n\n\nA F#m F G A\nTime and time and time again\nA F#m F G A\nI look to me my only friend\nA Bm\nTime and time and time again\nD A\nAre you here for my pleasure\nA Bm\nOr are you going for gold\nD E D C#m Bm\nAre you going for gold\n\n[Interlude]\nA D / A D / A D\nA F#m F G A\n\n[Verse 2]\nA D\nI never said never ever\nA D\nYou took the shine right out of my smile\nA D\nIs the moon your nighttime\nA D\nHave you been sold\nD\nThe moon is your lifeline\nG D\nGoing for gold\nG\nYou took the shine right out of my smile\n\n\nA D E A\nA D / A D / A D\n",
  "Shelley Duvall - He Needs Me": "Intro\nD Aaug D A D Aaug D A\n\nVerse 1\nD A\nAnd all at once I knew\nD\nI knew at once\nA\nI knew he needed me\nB F# B F#\n\nVerse 2\nD A\nUntil the day I die\nD\nI won't know why\n\nI knew he needed me\nB F# B F#\n\nVerse 3\nE B E Esus4 A\nIt could be fantasy, oh\nE A\nOr maybe it's because\nE A / He\n\nVerse 4\nD A\nneeds me, he needs me\nD\nHe needs me, he needs me\nA B G\nHe needs me, he needs me\nD\nHe needs me, he needs me\nA B G\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nInterlude 1\nB E\nB E B E A E A E A\nD A# D A\n\nVerse 5\nD A\nIt's like a dime a dance\nD\nI'll take a chance\nAaug A B\nI will because he need\nF#\ns me\nB F#\n\nVerse 6\nD\nNo one ever\nA D / asked before / A\nBefore because they\nB\nnever needed me\n\n(But I do)\nF# E\nBut he does\nB E\nMaybe it's because he's\n\nVerse 7\nB E A\nso alone\nE\nMaybe it's because he's\nA Esus4 E\nnever had a home\n\nVerse 8\nD\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nHe needs me, he needs me\nG B F# B\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nVerse 9\nD A\nFor once, for once in life\nD\nI've finally felt\nA B F# B F#\nThat someone needed me\nE B Em E Esus4\nAnd if it turns out real\nA Em A\nThen love can turn the wheel\nEm A / Because\n\nVerse 10\nD\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nHe needs me, he needs me\nB F# B\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nVerse 11\nD\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nHe needs me, he needs me\nB\nHe needs me, he needs me\n\nOutro\nB F# E B E B E A Em\nA Em D A D\nA D A Aaug D A D A Aaug D\nA D D\n",
  "Suede - Animal Nitrate": "[Intro]\nBm A G Em x4\n\n[Verse]\n     Bm   A       G              Em\nLike his dad you know that he's had\nBm         A       G         Em\nanimal nitrate in mind\n              Bm     A       G              Em\nOh in your council home he jumped on your bones\n            Bm         A         G\nnow you're taking it time after time\n\n[Chorus]\n                 D   G    D   G     Bm  A       G\nOh it turns you ooo-oon, ooo-oon... now he has gone\n                   D   G    D   G     Bm       A      F C\nOh what turns you ooo-oon, ooo-oon, now your animal's gone?\n\n[Verse]\n     Bm   A       G              Em\nWell he said he'd show you his bed\n           Bm               A       G       Em\nand the delights of the chemical smile\n            Bm      A       G              Em\nSo in your broken home he broke all your bones\n                 Bm        A         G\nand now you're taking it time after time\n\n[Chorus]\n                 D   G    D   G     Bm  A       G\nOh it turns you ooo-oon, ooo-oon... now he has gone\n                   D   G    D   G     Bm  A           F C\nOh what turns you ooo-oon, ooo-oon, now your animal's gone?\n\n[Solo]\nBm G E/G# G x3\nBm G G#   A\n\n[Chorus]\n                               D   G    D   G     Bm  A       G\nWhat does it take to turn you ooo-oon, ooo-oon... now he has gone?\n                       D   G    D   G   Bm        A       G\nnow you're over twenty-oo-one, oo-one? now your animal's gone?\n\n[Outro]\n      D      G      D   G     Bm  A       G\n...Animal, he was animal, an animal...\n",
  "Super Furry Animals - Ohio Heat": "NTRO:- Em AM G F EM,\n AM G F EM\n\nAm G F Em\nSycamore trees blowing green in the distance\n Am G F Em\nShe sucked on her thumb in her beautiful jail\n Am G F Em D\nA sentence to serve as her dynasty blows up inside her balloon\nBm A G F#m\nSalty Maureen had a bun in the oven\n Bm A G F#m\nThe daughters of charity let out a sigh\n Bm A G F#m E\nAs she suffered they pleaded for mercy she needed a long time ago\n\nBRIDGE:-\n\nB\nA long time ago\nD\nIn the greenest cypress groves\nE\nWe were beaming golden glow\n\nCHOURUS:-\n\nEm\nOhio heat\nBm\nSweet as sugar from a beet\nD\nSleek as foxes in the street\nE\nEvolution seemed comple\n\nAm G F Em,\nAm G F Em\n\n2ND VERSE:-\n\nAm G F Em\nDay after day and hour upon hour\n Am G F Em\nShe counted the seconds till she could no more\n Am G F Em D\nAs she climbed through the window and lowered herself with some sheets all tied up\nBm A G F#m\nRan through the fields till the ocean got closer\nBm A G F#m\nFound a deserted and rusty old boat\n Bm A G F#m E\nAs she fled for her life she did capsize and die a long time ago\n\nBRIDGE:-\n\nB\nA long time ago\nD\nIn the greenest cypress groves\nE\nWe were beaming golden glow\n\nCHOURUS:-\n\nEm\nOhio heat\nBm\nSweet as sugar from a beet\nD\nSleek as foxes in the street\nE\nEvolution seemed comple\n\nBREAK:-\n\nCHOURUS:-\n\nEm\nOhio heat\nBm\nSweet as sugar from a beet\nD\nSleek as foxes in the street\nE\nEvolution seemed comple\n\nEm\nOhio heat\nBm\nBlowing bubblegums discreet\nD\nNow there's flowers on the street\nE\nWhere she smoked and skipped her feet\nEm Bm\nFrom time to time on the flying tiger line\nD E\nShe appears in my sleep when my dreams are lucid deep\n\nEm\nOhio heat\nBm\nSweet as sugar from a beet\nD\nSleek as foxes in the street\nE\nEvolution seemed comple\n\nEm A Bm\nOh..io heat\nEm A Bm\nOh..io heat\n",
  "Super Furry Animals - The Gift That Keeps Giving": "Gift that keeps giving\n\n--Verse--\n\n  C           Dm\nA parcel arrived:\n\n            Em                Dm\nIt was the gift that keeps giving.\n\n  C          Dm\nI opened it up.\n\n             Em               Dm\nand all the bells started ringing.\n\n  C          Dm\nGonna take you right back,\n\n       Em          Dm\nRight back to the begining\n\n--Chorus--\n\n       Bb              F      C\nOf The gift that keeps givin again:\n\n          Bb             F      C\nIt's the Gift that keeps giving again.\n\n\n--Rest of Lyrics--\n\nWell before I received,\nThis gift that keeps on giving.\nI was always perceived as a loser,\nThat kept losing.\nWell look at me now,\nI'm a reciever that's reciving.\nAll these gifts that keeps giving again.\nIt's the gift that keeps giving again.\n\nGiving the gift that keeps giving again.\nIt's the gift that keeps giving again.\n\nGive it again, give it again, give it again.\nGive it again, give it again.\n\nGiving the gifts that keeps giving again.\nIt's the gift that keeps giving again.\nIt's the gift that keeps giving.\nRecievers keep receiving.\nIt's the gift that keeps giving again\n",
  "Terence Trent D'Arby - Sign Your Name": "\n[Intro]\nF#m x 2, B x 2, F#m x 2, B x 2, E, C#7/F\n \n[Verse 1]\nC# C#7/F\nFortunately you have \nF#m\nSomeone who relies on you \nC# C#7/F\nWe started out as friends \nF#m\nBut the thought of you just caves me in \nC# C#7/F\nThe symptoms are so deep \nF#m\nIt is much too late to turn away \nC# C#7/F C#7/F...\nWe started out as friends \n \n[Chorus]\nF#m\nSign your name across my heart \nB\nI want you to be my baby \nF#m\nSign your name across my heart \nB\nI want you to be my lady \nE C#7/F\n \n[Verse 2]\nC# C#7/F\nTime I'm sure will bring \nF#m\nDisappointments in so many things \nC# C#7/F\nIt seems to be the way \nF#m\nWhen you’re gambling cards on love you play \nC# C#7/F F#m\nI'd rather be in Hell with you baby \n \nThan in cool Heaven\nC# C#7/F C#7/F...\nIt seems to be the way \n \n[Chorus]\n \n[Bridge]\nD A C#\nBirds never look into the sun \nF#m\nBefore the day is gone \nD A\nBut oh the light shines brighter \nC# C#\nOn a peaceful day \nD A C#\nStranger blue leave us alone \nF#m\nWe don't want to deal with you \nD A\nWe'll shed our stains showering \nC# C# C# C#\nIn the room that makes the rain \n \nRepeat Intro:\nF#m F#m B B F#m F#m B B E C#7/F\n \n[Verse 3]\nC# C#7/F\nAll alone with you \nF#m\nMakes the butterflies in me arise \nC# C#7/F\nSlowly we make love \nF#m\nAnd the Earth rotates to our dictates \nC# C#7/F C#7/F NC NC NC NC\nSlowly we make love Hey.....\n \n[Chorus]\nF#m\nSign your name across my heart \nB\nI want you to be my baby \nF#m\nSign your name across my heart \nB\nI want you to be my lady \n(repeat to fade)\n",
  "The Cure - Boys Don't Cry": "[Intro]\nA Bm C#m D | D C#m Bm A\n \n[Verse]\nA                    Bm\nI would say I’m sorry\n        C#m                         D\nIf I thought that it would change your mind\nA                      Bm\nBut I know that this time\n      C#m\nI’ve said too much\n        D\nBeen too unkind \n \nC#m              Bm\n     I try to laugh about it\nC#m                     Bm\nCover it all up with lies\nC#m\n     I try and\nBm\nLaugh about it\nC#m                        Bm\nHiding the tears in my eyes\n \n[Chorus]\n                  A Bm C#m D D C#m Bm A\n'cause boys don’t cry\n A     Bm   C#m D D C#m Bm A\nBoys don’t cry \n \n[Verse]\nA                  Bm\nI would break down at your feet\n    C#m\nAnd beg forgiveness\nD\nPlead with you\nA\nBut I know that\nBm\nIt’s too late\n    C#m                  D\nAnd now there’s nothing I can do \nC#m               Bm\n   So I try to laugh about it\nC#m                       Bm\nCover it all up with lies\nC#m\nI try to\nBm\nlaugh about it\nC#m                      Bm\nHiding the tears in my eyes\n \n[Chorus]\n A Bm C#m D D C#m Bm A\n'cause boys don’t cry\n A     Bm   C#m D D C#m Bm A\nBoys don’t cry\n",
  "The Cure - Friday I'm in Love": "[Verse 1]\nD               G\nI don't care if Monday's blue\nD                  A\nTuesday's grey and Wednesday too\nBm              G\nThursday, I don't care about you\n     D              A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Verse 2]\nD               G\nMonday, you can fall apart\nD                   A\nTuesday, Wednesday, break my heart\nBm             G\nThursday doesn't even start\n     D              A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Chorus]\nG         A\nSaturday, wait\nBm              G\nAnd Sunday always comes too late\n    D             A\nBut Friday, never hesitate...\n\n[Verse 3]\nD               G\nI don't care if Monday's black\nD                   A\nTuesday, Wednesday, heart attack\nBm            G\nThursday, never looking back\n     D              A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Interlude]\nD  G  D  A  Bm  G  D  A\n\n[Verse 4]\nD               G\nMonday, you can hold your head\nD                   A\nTuesday, Wednesday, stay in bed\n   Bm                G\nOr Thursday, watch the walls instead\nD                   A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Chorus]\nG         A\nSaturday, wait\nBm              G\nAnd Sunday always comes too late\n    D             A\nBut Friday, never hesitate...\n\n[Bridge]\nBm                Cadd9                     D\nDressed up to the eyes, it's a wonderful surprise\n            A                       Bm\nTo see your shoes and your spirits rise\n                   Cadd9                        D\nThrowing out your frown and just smiling at the sound\n                   A\nAnd as sleek as a shriek spinning round and round\nBm                Cadd9                      D\nAlways take a big bite, it's such a gorgeous sight\n         A                          Bm\nTo see you eat in the middle of the night\n                    Cadd9                D\nYou can never get enough, enough of this stuff\n            A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Repeat Verse 1]\nD               G\nI don't care if Monday's blue\nD                  A\nTuesday's grey and Wednesday too\nBm              G\nThursday, I don't care about you\n     D              A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Repeat Verse 2]\nD               G\nMonday, you can fall apart\nD                   A\nTuesday, Wednesday, break my heart\nBm             G\nThursday doesn't even start\n     D              A\nIt's Friday, I'm in love\n\n[Outro]\nD  G  D  A  Bm  G  D  A  x2\n",
  "The Darkness - Get Your Hands off My Woman": "No capo\n\n\nD\nYou are drunk and surly\nF G\nIn Latino lover mode\nD\nWe all know what's on your agenda\nF G\nWe've broken the code\n\nG G F G G G F G\nI've got no right to lay claim to her frame\n G G F G\nShe's not my possession\n Em F F# G Ab A Bb B\nYou cunt.\n\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\n\nD\nOctoped, you've got six hands too many\nF G\nAnd you can't keep them to yourself\nD\nYou're too fat and too old to marry\nF G\nSo they left you on the shelf\n\nG G F G G G F G\nI've got no right to lay claim to her frame\n G G F G\nBut you soiled my obsession\n Em F F# G Ab A Bb B\nYou cunt.\n\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\n\nOw! (Solo Time)\n\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\nD Bb F C D Bb F C\nGet your hands off my woman motherfucker\n",
  "The Darkness - Givin' Up": "B F#\n\n\n[Verse 1]\nB\nMy mama wants to know\nB\nWhere I'm spending all my dough\nF#\nHoney, all she does is nag, nag, nag\nB\nBut I won't apologize\nB\nI'd inject into my eyes\nF#\nIf there was nowhere else to stick my skag\nB\nAll I want is brown\nB\nAnd I'm going into town\nF#\nShooting up as soon as I'm back\nB\nMy friends have got some good shit\nB\nAll I want is some of it\n F# G# B\nGimme, gimme, gimme that smack\n\n\nF# E\nWell, I've ruined nearly all of my veins\nF# E\nSticking that fucking shit into my arms\nE\nYeah-yeah\n\n\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nF# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\n F# G# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\n\n\n[Verse 2]\nB\nGetting off my face\nB\nThere's a dragon I must chase\nB\nHoney, I'm the scourge of all mankind\nB\nAnd everyone but me\nB\nIs destined just to be\nB\nSlaves to the remorseless grind\n\n\nF# E\nBut I found myself an easy way out\nF# E\nSticking that fucking shit into my arms\nE\nInto my arms\n\n\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nF# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\n F# G# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\n\n\n[Guitar solo]\nB E B G B\nF# B E F# E F# E\n\n\n[Out-Chorus]\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nF# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nF# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nF# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\nB\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nF# B\nGivin' up, givin' up givin' a fuck\n",
  "The Darkness - Growing on Me": "No capo\nGo!\n\n\n[Verse 1]\nD A Bm\n I can't get rid of you\nD A Bm A D\n I don't know what to do\nD A Bm A\n I don't even know who is growing on who\nG D\n Yeah-yeah\nD A Bm\n 'Cause everywhere I go, you're there\nD A Bm A D\n I can't get you out of my hair\nD A Bm A\n I can't pretend that I don't care\nEm\nIt's not fair\n\n\nG D A D\nI'm being punished for all my offences\nG D A D\nI want to touch you, but I'm afraid of the consequences\nG D A D\nI want to banish you from whence you came\n A D G\nBut you're part of me now, and I've only got myself to blame\n\n\nA D Bm G\nYou're really growing on me (Or am I growing on you?)\nA D G A D\nYou're really growing on me (Or am I growing on you?)\nA\nAny fool can see\n\n\n[Verse 2]\nD A Bm\n Sleepin' in an empty bed\nD A Bm A D\n I can't get you off my head\nD A Bm A\n And I won't have a life until you're dead\nEm\nYeah, you heard what I said\n\n\nG D A D\nI wanna shake you off, but you just won't go, oh\nG D A D\nAnd you're all over me, but I don't want anyone to know\nG D A D\nThat you're attached to me, that's how you've grown\n A D G\nWon't you leave me, leave me, leave me alone?\n\n\nA D Bm G\nYou're really growing on me (Or am I growing on you?)\nA D Bm G A D\nYou're really growing on me (Or am I growing on you?)\nA\nAny fool can see\n\n\nD G A D x5\nG\n\n\nA D Bm G\nYou're really growing on me (Or am I growing on you?)\nA D Bm G\nYou're really growing on me (Or am I growing on you?)\n",
  "The Darkness - Holding My Own": "No capo\n\nD Bm D D5 D Bm7 A G D Bm7 A G D Bm D G\nOooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooh\n\n\n[Verse 1]\nD Bm D\nBaby, everything has fallen into place.\nG G\nMy life is so exciting now I've got my space,\nBm7 D G\nLike a splash of water on my face Oooohooh.\nD Bm7 Asus4\nLately I'm doing what I can to pleasure me.\nA G D\nI'm finding time to focus on my fantasies.\n Bm7 Asus4 A\nI'm satisfied in my own company.\nG\nOoohoohoohoooo\n\n\nA A\nI don't need your permission\n Bm B G\nTo take this matter in my own two hands.\n\n\n Bm A G A\n'Cause I'm holding my own.\nD A G\nGive or take a tear or two, yeah.\nBm A G A\nI'm holding my own.\nD G\nNo matter what I put myself through.\n\n\nD Bm7 A G\n\n\n[Verse 2]\nD Bm7 A\nLady, all we seem to do is talk about.\nG D\nWe take apart and analyse our ins and outs.\nBm7 A G\nHoney, I would rather do without, yeah.\n\n\nA A\nNo one to answer to,\nG D G\nI won't spend another lifetime begging you.\n\n\n Bm A G A\n'Cause I'm holding my own.\nD A G\nGive or take a tear or two, yeah.\nBm A G A\nI'm holding my own.\n D A G\nNo matter what I put myself through.\nBm A D A\nI'm holding my own.\n\n\nG Em D A Bm A7sus4 A A7sus4 G A\n\n\nD Bm7 A G Em D Bm A G\n\n\nA\nThere's a spring in my stride.\nG D G\nThere's a twinkle in my dying eyes.\n\n\n Bm A G A\n'Cause I'm holding my own.\nD A G\nGive or take a tear or two, yeah.\nBm A G A\nI'm holding my own.\n D A G\nNo matter what I put myself through.\n\n\nBm A G A D A G x4\nBm D\n",
  "The Darkness - I Believe in a Thing Called Love": "[Verse 1]\n\nF#m A B E B A\nCan't explain all the feelings that you're making me feel\nF#m A B E B A\nMy heart's in overdrive and you're behind the steering wheel\n\n\nE F#m\n Touching you\nE F#m\n Touching me\nE F#m\n Touching you,\n A A# B\nGod you're touching me\n\n\nE A\nI believe in a thing called love\nF#m B\nJust listen to the rhythm of my heart\nE A\nThere's a chance we could make it now\nF#m B\nWe'll be rocking 'til the sun goes down\nE A F#m B\nI believe in a thing called lo-ve\nC#m D\nOoOOOOOh! Huh!\n\n\n[Solo 1]\n\nF#m A B E B A\n\n\n[Verse 2]\n\nF#m N.C. E B A\n I wanna kiss you every minute, every hour, every day\nF#m N.C. E B A\n You got me in a spin but everythin' is A-OK!\n\n\nE F#m\n Touching you\nE F#m\n Touching me\nE F#m\n Touching you,\n A A# B\nGod you're touching me\n\n\nE A\nI believe in a thing called love\nF#m B\nJust listen to the rhythm of my heart\nE A\nThere's a chance we could make it now\nF#m B\nWe'll be rocking 'til the sun goes down\nE A F#m B\nI believe in a thing called lo-ve\nC#m D\nOoOOOOOh! Guitar!\n\n\n[Solo 2]\n\nF#m A B E B A x4\n\n\nE F#m\n Touching you\nE F#m\n Touching me\nE F#m\n Touching you,\n A A# B\nGod you're touching me, ahhhhhh!\n\n\nE A\nI believe in a thing called love\nF#m B\nJust listen to the rhythm of my heart\nE A\nThere's a chance we could make it now\nF#m B\nWe'll be rocking 'til the sun goes down\nE A F#m B\nI believe in a thing called lo-ve\nC#m D\nOoOOOOOh! Huh!\n\n\n[Solo 3]\n\nE A F#m B x4\n\n\nE A F#m B x4, E\n",
  "The Darkness - Love Is Only a Feeling": "Bm G D A x4\n\n[Verse 1]\n G D A G\nThe first flush of youth was upon you when our eyes first met\n G D A\nAnd I knew that to you and into your life I had to get\n G D A G\nI felt light-headed at the touch of this stranger's hand\n G D A\nAn assault my defences systematically failed to withstand\n\n[Pre-chorus 1]\nEm\n'Cos you came at a time\nA\nWhen the pursuit of one true love in which to fall\nEm\nWas the be all and end all\n\n\nBm G D\nLove is only a feeling\nA\n(Drifting away)\nBm G D\nWhen I'm in your arms I start believing\nA\n(It's here to stay)\nBm G D\nBut love is only a feeling\nA / Anyway\n\nBm G D A x2\n\n[Verse 2]\n G D A G\nThe state of elation that this unison of hearts achieved\n G D A\nI had seen, I had touched, I had tasted and I truly believed\n\n[Pre-chorus 2]\nEm\nThat the light of my life\nA\nWould tear a hole right through each cloud that scudded by\nEm\nJust to beam on you and I\n\n\nBm G D\nLove is only a feeling\nA\n(Drifting away)\nBm G D\nWhen I'm in your arms I start believing\nA\n(It's here to stay)\nBm G D\nBut love is only a feeling\nA / Anyway\n\n(Solo)\n\n\nBm G D\nLove is only a feeling\nA\n(Drifting away)\nBm G D\nAnd we've got to stop ourselves believing\nA\n(It's here to stay)\nBm G D\n'cos love is only a feeling\nA / Anyway\n",
  "The Darkness - Stuck in a Rut": "A\n\n\n[Verse 1]\nA\nWell, kiss my ass, kiss my ass goodbye\nA\nPropelled by a carriage of aluminium, am I\nD\nNo more to rot in this sty\nD\nI'd turn my back on this shit-hole in the blink of an eye, ow!\n\n\nD\nGimme the keys\nA D\nYou ain’t gonna see me for dust\nA\nThe Barnby Bends ain't gonna get the better of me\nD\nOh, gimme the keys\nA\nTo any old bucket of rust\nD A\nAcle Straight gonna take me to where I wanna be\n\n\nG\nStuck in a rut\n A D G\nStuck in a rut for eternity\nA D\nStuck in a rut\nA G D G A\nStuck in a rut for eternity, yeah\n\n\n[Verse 2]\nA\nWell, the road is long, and the lights are bright\nA\nJust 'cause you've lived here all your life, doesn't make it alright\nD A\nAnd the golden mile is paved with shite\nA\nDon't mind telling you\nA\nI'm sick of walking up and down it, every single fucking night\n\n\nD\nJust gimme the keys\nA\nYou ain’t gonna see me for dust\nD A\nThe Barnby Bends ain't gonna get the better of me\nD\nOh, gimme the keys\nA D\nTo any old bucket of rust\nA D\nAcle Straight gonna take me to where I wanna be, yeah yeah\n\n\nA D\nStuck in a rut\n A D G\nStuck in a rut for eternity, ow!\nD\nStuck in a rut\nG D G A\nStuck in a rut for eternity, yeah\n\n\nA\nMaster?\n F D A\nKill me, Master, kill me\nF\nOoh, thank you, Master\nF\nThank you, Master\n E D# D\n[Maniacal laughter]\n\n\n[Guitar solo]\nG A G\nE A D A D\nD A D\n\n\n[Out-Chorus]\nA D\nStuck in a rut\nG E G\nStuck in a rut for eternity, oh\nA D\nStuck in a rut\nG A D A G A G A G A G\nStuck in a rut for eternity, yeah-ow\n",
  "The Monkees - Me & Magdelana": "G C C G x4\n\n[Verse 1]\nC G/B\nMe and Magdelena\n G C G\nWe're driving south through Monterey\nC G/B\nAs the sun is slowly sinking\n G C G\nInto a distant ocean wave\n\n\nD\nAnd I don't know if I've\nC G\never loved any other\nD\nHalf as much as I do\n C G C G\nin this light she's under\n\n[Verse 2]\nC G/B\nTell me Magdelena\n\nWhat do you see in the\nG C G\ndepths of your night?\nC G/B\nDo you see your long lost father?\n\nDoes he hold you with the hands\n G C G\nYou remember as a child?\nD\nBut know everything lost\nC G\nwill be recovered\nD\nWhen we drift into the arms\nC G\nof the undiscovered\n\n\nEm\nAnd I don't know if I've\nC G\never loved any other\nD\nHalf as much as I do\n C G C G\nin this light she's under\n\n[Verse 3]\nC G/B\nMe and Magdelena\n G C G\nAlways leaving early and sleeping late\nC G/B\nSecluded in the canyon\n G C G\nLost within a turn of fate\nD\nBut now everything lost\nC G\nwill be recovered\nD\nWhen you drift into the arms\nC G\nof the undiscovered\n\n\nEm\nAnd I don't know if I've\nC G\never loved any other\nD\nHalf as much as I do\nC G\nin this light she's under\n",
  "The Offspring - Come Out And Play (Keep 'Em Separated)": "[Intro]\n\nE\n\nB D F# A (x8)\n\nB F# A  B F# D (x3)\n\nB F# A B\n\nN.C.\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\n\n\n[Verse]\n\nB                F#  A  B      D F# A\nThey're like the latest fashion\nB              F#   A    B      D F# A\nThey're like a spreading disease\nB            F#  A        B                         D F# A\nThe kids are strappin' on their way to the classroom\nB       F# A    B                        D F# A\nGetting weapons with the greatest of ease\n\n\n[Pre-chorus]\n\n    E2          G2        F#2      B   D2\nThe gangs stake their own campus locale\n    E2                G2                F#2      B  D2\nAnd if they catch you slippin' then it's all over pal\n   B        F#          A   B           D   F# A\nIf one guy's colors and the others don't mix\n        F#\nThey're gonna bash it up, bash it up, bash it up, bash it up\n\n\n[Chorus]\n\nB D  F#  A   B       D    F# A\nHey, man you talkin' back to me?\nB         D\n Take him out\nF#  A     B\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\nB D  F#  A   B     D F#    A\nHey, man you disrespecting me?\nB        D\n Take him out\nF#  A     B\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\nB D  F#   A     B      D\nHey, they don't pay no mind\nF# A      E2                    C\nIf you're under 18 you won't be doing any time\nB D F# A F#             B D F# A B\nHey,       come out and play!\n\n\n[Bridge]\n\nB F# A B F# D (x3)\n\nB F# A B\n\n\n[Verse]\n\nB      F#       A        B    D F# A\nBy the time you hear the siren\nB      F#    A   B   D F# A\nIt's already too late\nB               F#     A       B            D F# A\nOne goes to the morgue and the other to jail\nB         F#     A       B              D F# A\nOne guy's wasted and the other's a waste\n\n\n[Pre-chorus]\n\nE2               G2          F#2      B D2\nIt goes down the same as the thousand before\nE2               G2                F#2      B   D2\nNo one's getting smarter, no one's learning the score\nB                 F#       A         B        D   F#  A\nYour never ending spree of death and violence and hate\n   F#\nIs gonna tie your own rope, tie your own rope, tie your own\n\n\n[Chorus]\n\nB D  F#  A   B       D    F# A\nHey, man you talkin' back to me?\nB         D\n Take him out\nF#  A     B\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\nB D  F#  A   B     D F#    A\nHey, man you disrespecting me?\nB        D\n Take him out\nF#  A     B\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\nB D  F#   A     B      D\nHey, they don't pay no mind\nF# A      E2                    C\nIf you're under 18 you won't be doing any time\nB D F# A F#             B D F# A B\nHey,       come out and play!\n\n\n[Bridge]\n\nB F# A B F# D (x3)\n\nB F# A B\n\n\n[Pre-chorus]\n\nE2               G2          F#2      B D2\nIt goes down the same as the thousand before\nE2               G2                F#2      B   D2\nNo one's getting smarter, no one's learning the score\nB                 F#       A         B        D   F#  A\nYour never ending spree of death and violence and hate\n   F#\nIs gonna tie your own rope, tie your own rope, tie your own\n\n\n[Chorus]\n\nB D  F#  A   B       D    F# A\nHey, man you talkin' back to me?\nB         D\n Take him out\nF#  A     B\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\nB D  F#  A   B     D F#    A\nHey, man you disrespecting me?\nB        D\n Take him out\nF#  A     B\nYou gotta keep 'em separated\nB D  F#   A     B      D\nHey, they don't pay no mind\nF# A      E2                    C\nIf you're under 18 you won't be doing any time\nB D F# A F#             B D F# A B\nHey,       come out and play!\n",
  "The Shins - Australia": "E C#m F#m\nBorn to multiply or born to gaze into night skies,\nF#m G#m A G#m F#m\n all you want's one more Saturday.\nE C#m\nBut look here, until then\nF#m\nThey're gonna buy your life's time\nF#m G#m A G#m F#m\n So keep your wick in the air and your feet in the fetters\n\n\nB E\nTil the day, we come in doing cartwheels\nB E\nWe all crawl out by ourselves, and your shape on the dance floor\nB\nWill have me thinking such filth I'll gouge my eyes.\nC#m A\nYou'll be damned to be one of us girl\nC#m A\nFaced with the dodo's conundrum\nE F#m A\n I felt like I could just fly\n G#m B A G#m F#m\nBut nothing happened every time I tried.\n\n\nE C#m F#m\nDuotone on the wall, the selfless fool who hoped he'd saved us all\nF#m G#m A G#m F#m\n never dreamt of such sterile hands\nE C#m F#m\nYou keep them folded in your lap, or raise them up to beg for scraps\nF#m G#m A G#m F#m B\nYou know he's holding you down with the tips of his fingers, just the same\n\n\nE B\nWill you be pulled from the ocean? But just a minute too late?\nE B\nOr changed by a potion, and find a handsome young mate for you to love\nC#m A\nyou'll be damned to pining through the window panes, you know\nC#m A E F#m A\nyou'll trade your life for any ordinary joe's, well do it now or grow old\n G#m B A G#m F#m\nCos your nightmares only need a year or two to unfold\n\n\nE C#m F#m G#m A G#m F#m x2\n\n\nB E\nBeen alone since you were 21, you haven't laughed since January\nB E\nYou try and make like this is so much fun, but we know it to be be quite contrary\nB\nLa la la la la la\n\n\nC#m A C#m A\nDare to be one of us, girl, facing the android's conundrum\nE F#m A\n I felt like I should just cry\nG#m A\nBut nothing happens every time I take one on the chin\nG#m A\nYeah Himmler in your coat you don't know how long I've been\nG#m A G#m A\nWatching the lantern dim, starved of oxygen, oh\n F#m A B\nso give me your hand and lets jump out the window\n\n\nE\n",
  "The Shins - Phantom Limb": "[Verse 1]\nA D\nFoals in winter coats\nBm\nWhite girls of the North\nG D\nFile past; one, five, and one\nD\nThey are the fabled lambs\nE\nOf Sunday ham\nBm\nThe EHS norm\n\n[Verse 2]\nA D\nAnd they could float above the grass\nA\nIn circles if they tried\nG D\nA latent power I know they hide\nD\nTo keep some hope alive\nE\nThat a girl like I\nBm\nCould ever try\nA\nCould ever try\n\n[Chorus 1]\n F#m D E\nSo we just skirt the hallway sides\nF#m\nA phantom and a fly\nF# D\nFollow the lines\nE\nAnd wonder why\nE\n There's no connection\n\n[Verse 3]\nA D\nA week of rolling eyes\nBm\nAnd cheap shots from the tribe\nG D\nAnd we're off to Nemarca's porch again\nD / Another afternoon / E\nOf the goat-head tunes\nBm\nAnd pilfered booze\nA D\nWe wander through her Momma's house\nA\nThe milk from the window lights\nG D\nFamily portrait, circa '95\nD\nThis is that foreign land\nE\nWith the sprayed-on tans\nBm\nAnd it all feels fine\nA\nBe it silk or slime\n\n[Chorus 2]\nF#m D E\nSo, when they tap our Monday heads\nF#m\nTwo zombies walk in our stead\nF# D E\nThis town seems hardly worth our time\n F#m D E\nAnd we'll no longer memorize or rhyme\nF#m\nToo far along in our crime\n F# D E\nStepping over what now towers to the sky\nE\n With no connection\n\n\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh, ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh, ohh\n\n[Chorus 3]\nF#m D E\nSo, when they tap our Sunday heads\nF#m\nTwo zombie walk in our stead\nF# D E\nThis town seems hardly worth our time\n F#m D E\nAnd we'll no longer memorize or rhyme\nF#m\nToo far along in our crime\n F# D E\nStepping over what now towers to the sky\nE\n With no connection\n\n\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh, ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh, ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh\nA D E\nOh, oh-oh, oh-ohh, ohh\n",
  "The Shins - Sleeping Lessons": "Go without 'til the need seeps in\nA E\nyou're low anymore; collect your novel petals for the stem\nE\nand glow, glow; melt and flow\n\n\nE\neviserate your fragile frame\nA E\nspilled it all in ragged form; a thousand different versions of yourself\nB A\n and if the old gaurd still offend; you got nothing left on which you depend\nA\nso enlist every ounce of your bright blood and off with their heads\n\n\nE A\n Jump from the book; you're not obliged to swallow anything you despise\n\n\nE\nSee those unrepenting buzzards want your life\nA\nwhen they got no right; as sure as you have eyes\n E B A\nthey got no right\n\n\nE A\n\nE\nJust put yourself in my new shoes; and see that I do what I do\nB A\nbecause the old gods still offend; we got nothing left on which we depend\nA\nso we waste every ounce of your bright blood and off with their heads\n\n\nE\n Jump from the book; you're not obliged to swallow anything you despise\n",
  "The Smiths - I Don't Owe You Anything": "Dmaj7 B\nEmaj7 ...\n\n\n[Verse 1]\nEmaj7\nBought on stolen wine\n\nA nod was the first step\nAmaj7\nYou knew very well\nB Emaj7\nWhat was coming next\n\nBought on stolen wine\n\nA nod was the first step\nAmaj7\nYou knew very well\nB Emaj7\nWhat was coming next\n\n\n Amaj7 B Emaj7\nDid I really walk all this way\nDmaj7 B Emaj7\nJust to hear you say:\n Amaj7 B Emaj7\n\"Oh, I don't want to go out tonight\"\n Dmaj7 B C#m7\n\"Oh, I don't want to go out tonight\"\n\nOh, but you will\n Dmaj7 B Emaj7\nFor you must\nG#m A Emaj7 A\nI don't owe you anything, no\nG#m A\nBut you owe me something\nDmaj7 B\nRepay me now\n\n\n[Verse 2]\nEmaj7\nYou should never go to them\n\nLet them come to you\nAmaj7 B\nJust like I do\nEmaj7\nJust like I do\n\nYou should not go to them\n\nLet them come to you\nAmaj7 B\nJust like I do\nEmaj7\nJust like I do\n\n\n Amaj7 B Emaj7\nDid I really walk all this way\nDmaj7 B Emaj7\nJust to hear you say:\n Amaj7 B Emaj7\n\"Oh, I don't want to go out tonight\"\n Dmaj7 B C#m7\n\"Oh, I don't want to go out tonight\"\n\nOh, but you will\n Dmaj7 B Emaj7\nFor you must\nG#m A Emaj7 A\nI don't owe you anything, no\nG#m A\nBut you owe me something\nDmaj7 B\nRepay me now\n\n\n[Verse 3]\nEmaj7\nToo freely on your lips\n\nWords prematurely sad\n Amaj7 B Emaj7\nOh, but I know what will make you smile tonight\n\nLife is never kind\n\nLife is never kind\n Amaj7 B Emaj7\nOh, but I know what will make you smile tonight\n\n\nDmaj7 B Emaj7\n",
  "The Smiths - What Difference Does it Make?": "| B5 | % | D6 | E5 |\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n\n[Verse 1]\n\nB5 D E5 D B5\n All men have secrets and here is mine so let it be known\n D E5 D B5\nFor we have been through hell and high tide I think I can rely on you\n D E5 D B5\nAnd yet you start to recoil heavy words are so lightly thrown\n D E5 D\nBut still I'd leap infront of a flying bullet for you\n\n\nB5 E5 F# A\n So what difference does it make\nB5 E5 F# A\n So what difference does it make\nG#m E5 F# G#m E5\n It makes none but now you have gone\nF# G#m E5 F# B5\nAnd you must be looking very old tonight\n\n[Verse 2]\n\n D E5 D B5\nThe devil will find work for idle hands to do\n D E5 D B5\nI stole and I lied and why because you asked me to\n D E5 D B5\nBut now you make me feel so ashamed because I've only got two hands\n D E5 D\nWell I'm still fond of you oh ho hoh\n\n\nB5 E5 F# A\n So what difference does it make\nB5 E5 F# A\n What difference does it make\nG#m E5 F# G#m E5\n It makes none but now you have gone\nF# G#m E5 F# B5\nAnd your prejudice won't keep you warm tonight\n\n[Verse 3]\n\n D E5 D B5\nOh the devil will find work for idle hands to do\n D E5 D B5\nI stole and then I lied just because you asked me to\n D E5 D B5\nBut now you know the truth about me you won't see me anymore\n D E5 D\nWell I'm still fond of you oh ho hoh\n\n\nB5 E5 F# A B5 E5 F# A\n But no more apologies no more, no more apologies\nG#m E5 F# G#m E5\n Oh I'm too tired, I'm so sick and tired\nF# G#m E5 F# B5\nAnd I'm feeling very sick and ill today\n D E5 D\nBut I'm still fond of you oh ho hoh\n\n\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\nB5 D E5 D\n Oh, my sacred one\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n| B5 | % | D | E5 D |\n| B5 | % | B5\n",
  "The Stone Roses - Elizabeth My Dear": "CAPO 2nd fret\nAm\nTear me apart\n    Em      Am   C\nAnd boil my bones\n         Am\nI'll not rest\n     D              Am\n'Til she's lost her throne\n   F      C/E\nMy aim is true\n   G/D G/C G/B Gsus4 G\nMy message is clear\n     Am           D\nIt's curtains for you\nG Gsus G      Am\nElizabeth, my dear\n",
  "The Vaccines - All in White": "Capo 1\n \n[Verse]\nC#m                A            E\nBreak me on the thirty-seventh hour\nC#m                 A                   E\nTout me, doubt me, show me all of your power\nC#m               A                        E\nI will watch you rise on my back from the ground\nC#m                     A                              E\nFriend or foe? I don't know. Do you like what you've found?\n \n[Bridge]\nE       B       A          E\nI will one day shine with you\nE           B    A        E\nI'll shine on a faithful few\n \n[Chorus]\nE             C#m\nShow we 'low quotations\nA                      E\nHave you earned your stripes?\nE              C#m\nFabricate salvation\nA                  E\nLord, I know your type\n                      E B A E\nI've known you all my life\n                E    B   A       E\nI was always wrong, you all in white\n \n[Verse]\nC#m         A                       E\nBrush my cause aside with little trouble\nC#m           A                   E\nOh my god, I think I'm hearing double\nC#m               A                    E\nI will watch you rise on my back from afar\nC#m                     A                          E\nFriend or foe? I don't know, now you're up in the stars\n \n[Bridge]\n    E       B       A         E\nBut I will one day shine with you\nE           B    A       E\nI'll shine on a faithful few\n \n[Chorus] (x3)\nE              C#m\nShow we 'low quotations\nA                        E\nHave you earned your stripes?\nE          C#m\nFabricate salvation\nA                  E\nLord, I know your type\n                       E B A E\nI've known you all my life\n               E     B   A     E\nI was always wrong, you all in white\n",
  "The Wonder Stuff - Circle Square": "Eadd9add11 is a C chord slid two frets up, open.\nAsus13 is a D with the first finger moved up a string\nAadd9 is a Cadd9 on the 12th fret\nEadd11 is open G on the 12th fret\nDadd9 is open G on the 10th fret\n\n(Verse 1)\nEm                   Eadd9add11         Cadd9\nIs that a smile that hangs beneath your nose\nEm                          Eadd9add11          Cadd9\nOr are your lips just stuck to your teeth and they're too fixed to close\n          Em             Eadd9add11    Cadd9\nYou don't have to ham it up for me or tell me how long you've\nEm             Eadd9add11      Cadd9\nWaited just to be with me\n            D                           Asus13\nI've been a long term disappointment to myself\n       Aadd9                          Eadd11\nBut it hits like a hammer when I'm that to someone else\n            D                              Asus13\nAnd now the circle doesn't fit it's little square\n    Aadd9                       Eadd11\nIt bulges with opportunity ... bulges\n\n(Verse 2)\nEm                   Eadd9add11         Cadd9\nIs that a smile that hangs beneath your nose\nEm                          Eadd9add11          Cadd9\nOr are your eyes so wide they've pulled your mouth into a stupid pose\n          Em             Eadd9add11    Cadd9\nYou don't have to ham it up for me or tell me how long you've\nEm             Eadd9add11      Cadd9\nWaited just to be with me\n\n(Chorus)\n            D                           Asus13\nI've been a long term disappointment to myself\n       Aadd9                          Eadd11\nBut it hits like a hammer when I'm that to someone else\n            D                              Asus13\nAnd now the circle doesn't fit it's little square\n    Aadd9                       Eadd11\nIt bulges with opportunity ... bulges\n\n(Bridge)\nAadd9 Eadd11 Dadd9 Dadd9/Eadd11 Dadd9/Eadd11 Dadd9/Eadd11 x4\n\n(Chorus)\n            D                           Asus13\nI've been a long term disappointment to myself\n       Aadd9                          Eadd11\nBut it hits like a hammer when I'm that to someone else\n            D                           Asus13\nAnd now the circle doesn't fit it's little square\n    Aadd9                       Eadd11\nIt bulges with opportunity ... bulges\nx2\nD Asus13 x 4\n",
  "Tracy Chapman - Fast Car": "[Intro]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x4\n\n[Verse 1]\nCmaj7          G*\nYou got a fast car.\nEm7                 Dadd11\nI want a ticket to anywhere.\nCmaj7           G*\nMaybe we make a deal,\nEm7                    Dadd11\nMaybe together we can get somewhere.\nCmaj7             G*\nAny place is better.\nEm7                      Dadd11\nStarting from zero, got nothing to lose.\nCmaj7                 G*\nMaybe we'll make something,\nEm7               Dadd11\nMe myself, I got nothing to prove.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x2\n\n[Verse 2]\nCmaj7          G*\nYou got a fast car\nEm7                 Dadd11\nI got a plan to get us out of here:\nCmaj7           G*\nI been working at the convenience store,\nEm7                 Dadd11\nManaged to save just a little bit of money.\nCmaj7          G*\nWont't have to drive too far\nEm7                 Dadd11\nJust across the border and into the city,\nCmaj7          G*\nYou and I can both get jobs\nEm7                 Dadd11\nAnd finally see what it means to be living.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x2\n\n[Verse 3]\nCmaj7          G*\nYou see my old man's got a problem:\nEm7                 Dadd11\nHe live with the bottle, that's the way it is.\nCmaj7          G*\nHe says his body's too old for working,\nEm7                 Dadd11\nHis body's too young to look like his.\nCmaj7          G*\nMy mama went off and left him,\nEm7                     Dadd11\nshe wanted more from life than he could give,\nCmaj7               G*\nI said, \"Somebody's got to take care of him.\"\nEm7                Dadd11\nSo I quit school and that's what I did.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x2\n\n[Verse 4]\nCmaj7  G*\nYou got a fast car\nEm7  Dadd11\nBut is it fast enough so we can fly away?\nCmaj7  G*\nWe gotta make a decision:\nEm7  Dadd11\nLeave tonight or live and die this way.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  Cmaj7  G*\n\n[Chorus]\nEm    Dadd11              C\n I remember when we were driving, driving in your car,\n     G\nThe speed so fast I felt like I was drunk,\nEm7\n  City lights lay out before us\n          D\nAnd your arm felt nice wrapped 'round my shoulder.\n    C   Em7      D\nAnd I_____ had a feeling that I belonged\n    C   Em7      D                           C         D\nAnd I_____ had a feeling I could be someone, be someone, be someone.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x2\n\n[Verse 5]\nCmaj7  G*\nYou got a fast car\n Em7  Dadd11\nAnd we go cruising to entertain ourelves;\nCmaj7  G*\nYou still ain't got a job\n Em7  Dadd11\nAnd I work in a market as a checkout girl.\nCmaj7  G*\nI know things will get better:\n Em7  Dadd11\nYou'll find work and I'll get promoted,\nCmaj7  G*\nWe'll move out of the shelter\n Em7  Dadd11\nBuy a bigger house and live in the suburbs.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  Cmaj7  G*\n\n[Chorus]\nEm    Dadd11              C\n I remember when we were driving, driving in your car,\n     G\nThe speed so fast I felt like I was drunk,\nEm7\n  City lights lay out before us\n          D\nAnd your arm felt nice wrapped 'round my shoulder.\n    C   Em7      D\nAnd I_____ had a feeling that I belonged\n    C   Em7      D                           C         D\nAnd I_____ had a feeling I could be someone, be someone, be someone.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x2\n\n[Verse 6]\nCmaj7  G*\nYou got a fast car\nEm7  Dadd11\nAnd I got a job that pays all our bills.\nCmaj7  G*\nYou stay out drinking late at the bar,\nEm7  Dadd11\nSee more your friends than you do your kids.\nCmaj7  G*\nI'd always hoped for better,\nEm7  Dadd11\nThought maybe together you and me would find it,\nCmaj7  G*\nI got no plans, I ain't going nowhere,\nEm7  Dadd11\nso take your fast car and keep on driving.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  Cmaj7  G*\n\n[Chorus]\nEm    Dadd11              C\n I remember when we were driving, driving in your car,\n     G\nThe speed so fast I felt like I was drunk,\nEm7\n  City lights lay out before us\n          D\nAnd your arm felt nice wrapped 'round my shoulder.\n    C   Em7      D\nAnd I_____ had a feeling that I belonged\n    C   Em7      D                           C         D\nAnd I_____ had a feeling I could be someone, be someone, be someone.\n\n[Instrumental]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x2\n\n[Verse 7]\nCmaj7  G*\nYou got a fast car\nEm7  Dadd11\nBut is it fast enough so you can fly away?\nCmaj7  G*\nYou gotta make a decision:\nEm7  Dadd11\nLeave tonight or live and die this way.\n\n[Outro]\nCmaj7  G*  Em7  Dadd11  x3\nCmaj7  G*\n",
  "Weezer - Buddy Holly": "[Verse 1]\n\nF#                               G# A\nWhat's with these homies dissin' my girl\nA\nWhy do they gotta front\nF#                           G# A\nWhat did we ever do to these guys\nA\nThat made them so violent\n\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n\nD                 C#m       F#\nOoh ooh, but you know I'm yours\nD                 C#m        F#\nOoh ooh, and you know you're mine\nD             Dm\nOoh ooh, and that's for all time\n\n\n[Chorus]\n\nA                    D              E\nOoh wee ooh, I look just like Buddy Holly\nA                   D         E\nUh oh, and you're Mary Tyler Moore\nF#                     D E A\nI don't care what they say about us anyway,\nA     D     E        A\nI don't care about that\n\n\n[Bridge 1]\n\n\n[Verse 2]\n\nF#                               G# A\nDon't you ever fear, I'm always near\nA\nI know that you need help\nF#                                     G# A\nYour tongue is twisted, your eyes are slit\nA\nYou need a guardian\n\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n\nD                 C#m       F#\nOoh ooh, but you know I'm yours\nD                 C#m        F#\nOoh ooh, and you know you're mine\nD             Dm\nOoh ooh, and that's for all time\n\n\n[Chorus]\n\nA                    D              E\nOoh wee ooh, I look just like Buddy Holly\nA                   D         E\nUh oh, and you're Mary Tyler Moore\nF#                     D E A\nI don't care what they say about us anyway,\nA     D     E        A\nI don't care about that\n\n\n[Bridge 2]\n(This is the part I didn't get yet that needs work)\n\nIt's mostly just A E F# E  with a little run.\n(The trick is to barre the F#, and let the E open by letting up your index\nfinger.\nWhen I get a chance I will fix it, unless someone gets to it first!)\n\nBang bang, knock on the door\n'Nother big bang, you're down on the floor\nOh no, what do we do\nDon't look down but I lost my shoe\nI can't run and I can't kick\nWhat's the matter babe, are you feelin' sick\nWhat's a matter, what's a matter, what's a matter, you\nWhat's a matter babe, are you feelin' blue\n\n[Solo]\n\n[Chorus]\n\nA                    D              E\nOoh wee ooh, I look just like Buddy Holly\nA                   D         E\nUh oh, and you're Mary Tyler Moore\nF#                     D E A\nI don't care what they say about us anyway,\nA     D     E        A\nI don't care about that\n",
  "Wild Beasts - All The King's Men": "Cadd9 Bb\nCadd9 Db Bb\n\nBbmaj7\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nBb6\nOh-oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh\nx2\nBbmaj7\nWatch me! watch me!\n                 Bb6\nThe belle of the ball\nBbmaj7\nMy heart, my hand\n                 Bb6\nAnd everything I own\n                Bbmaj7\nAnd we are the boys\n                 Bb6\nWith new shiny shoes\n                Bbmaj7\nWe've seen 'em all\n                 Bb6\nAnd we've chosen you\n    Gm7                    Bb\nNow no one will find your limit\n            Csus   Ebadd9\nGirls from Roedean\n            Bb\nGirls from Shipley\n            Csus   Ebadd9\nGirls from Hounslow\n            Bb\nGirls from Whitby\nYou're a candied queen\n    Csus   Ebadd9                    Bb\nAnd let me show my darling what that means\nWatch me! watch me!\nOoh-ooh\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh x4\n\nHatch me! hatch me!\nA girl before\nBouncing round\nBehind the bedroom doors\nAnd we are the boys\nWho'll drape you in jewels\nCut off your hair\nAnd throw out your shoes\n\nCause baby\nYou won't need them where you'll be\nGirls astride me\nGirls beneath me\nGirls before me\nGirls between me\nYou're birthing machines\nAnd let me show my darling what that means\nHatch me! Hatch me!\nOoh-ooh, ooh\nOh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh x4\n\nAnd baby\nTurns out I'm evil\nIn all my dreams, girls who'll clothe me\nGirls who'll feed me\nGirls who want me\nGirls who need me\nAll you pretty things waiting for somebody\nNumber my babies and my broken body\n",
  "a-ha - Take on Me": "Capo 2\n \n[Verse 1]\nAm           D\nTalking away\nG                C       C/B\nI don't know what I'm to say\n     Am            D\nI'll say it anyway\n  G              C      C/B\nToday's another day to find you\nAm         D\nShying away\nEm                      C\nI'll be coming for your love, okay\n \n[Chorus]\nG    D  Em  C\nTake on me (take on me)\nG    D  Em  C\nTake me on (take on me)\nG    D   Em  C             G  D/F#  C  D\nI'll be gone   in a day or two\n \n[Verse 2]\n   Am             D    G\nSo needless to say I'm odds and ends\nC         C/B  Am         D\n But I'll be-e stumbling away\nG                     C       C/B\nSlowly learning that life is okay\nAm           D\nSay after me\nEm                   C\nIt's no better to be safe than sorry\n \n[Chorus]\nG    D  Em  C\nTake on me (take on me)\nG    D  Em  C\nTake me on (take on me)\nG    D   Em  C             G  D/F#  C  D\nI'll be gone   in a day or two\n \n[Instrumental]\nBm        F       Bm       F      Am        D\nAm    D   Am   D\nAm    D   G     C  C/B\nAm    D   G     C  C/B\nAm    D   Am   D\n \n[Verse 3]\n        Am               D\nOh, the things that you say\nG            C        C/B\nIs it life or just to play\n   Am           D\nMy worries away\n       G                   C        C/B\nYou're all the things I've got to remember\nAm            D\nYou shying away\nEm                   C\nI'll be coming for you anyway\n \n[Chorus]\nG    D  Em  C\nTake on me (take on me)\nG    D  Em  C\nTake me on (take on me)\nG    D   Em  C      G  D/F#  C  D\nI'll be gone   in a day\n \nG    D  Em  C\nTake on me (take on me)\nG    D  Em  C\nTake me on (take on me)\nG    D   Em  C      G  D/F#  C  D\nI'll be gone   in a day\n",
  "Édith Piaf - La Vie en Rose": "G Am Cm G D\n\n\nG Gmaj7\nHold me close and hold me fast\nEm\nThis magic spell cast\nAm D\n\nAm D\nWhen you kiss me heaven sighs\nAm\nAnd though I close my eyes\n D G D\nI see la vie en ro-se\n\nG Gmaj7\nWhen you press me to your heart\nEm\nI'm in a world apart\nG C\nA world where roses bloom\n\nCm\nAnd when you speak\nG\nAngels sing from above\nA D\nEveryday words seem to turn into love songs\n\nG Gmaj7\nGive your heart and soul to me\n Am D C D G\nAnd life will always be la vie en rose\n\n\nG\nI thought love was just a word\nE Am\nThey sung a-bout in songs I heard\n D G Dm\nIt took your kisses to reveal\nE D\nThat I was wrong, and love is real\n\n\nG Gmaj7\nQuand il me prend dans ses bras\nEm\nIl me parle tout bas\nAm D\n\nAm D\nIl me dit des mots d'amour\nAm\nDes mots de tous le jours\n D G G#m D\nEt ça me fait quelque chose\n\nG Gmaj7\nIl est entré dans mon coeur\nEm\nUne part de bonheur\nG C\nDont je connais la cause\n\nCm\nC'est lui pour moi\nG\nMoi pour lui dans la vie\nA D\nIl me l'a dit, l'a juré pour la vie\n\nG\nEt dès que je l'aperçois\n Am D Am D G\nAlors je sens en moi, mon coeur qui bat ...\n\n\nG Gmaj7 Em Am D Am D G\nla la la...\n"
}
